---
/* THE PAGE THE FRONT PAGE KEPT FOLDING AWAY.
 *
 * Two panels of prose — why the atlas is a map, and what it does not know —
 * sat under the map behind a <details>. Folding them was the right call for
 * the front page and the wrong home for the text: a reader who has already
 * got the point scrolled past it every visit, and a reader who arrived with a
 * surname met an essay before they met an answer.
 *
 * So the text lives here, on a page somebody reaches by asking for help, and
 * it is allowed to be longer than a fold. The front page keeps the map.
 *
 * WHILE MOVING IT, TWO THINGS WERE WRONG AND ARE FIXED:
 *   · «Online is four different things» — it is eight, and the eighth is
 *     «nobody has looked», which is nine dots in ten.
 *   · The counts printed as 21473 and 2547650, unseparated, because the front
 *     page interpolated them raw.
 * Every number here is counted at build time.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import HomeAbout from "../components/HomeAbout.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { atlas as idx } from "../lib/atlas.js";
import regions from "../../public/regions.json";
import provs from "../../public/providers.json";

const places = idx.places.length;
const volumes = idx.places.reduce((a, p) => a + (p.v || 0), 0);
const archives = provs.providers.filter((p) => p.at);
const archiveCountries = new Set(archives.map((p) => p.at.place.split(", ").pop())).size;

const RANK = idx.rank || [];
const SURVEYED = new Set(["free", "account", "index", "mixed", "paid", "catalogue", "onsite"]);
const accessOf = (p) => (typeof p.a === "number" && RANK[p.a]) || "unsurveyed";
const surveyed = idx.places.filter((p) => SURVEYED.has(accessOf(p))).length;
const unsurveyedPct = Math.round((1 - surveyed / places) * 1000) / 10;

/* The access vocabulary, read from the index rather than restated, so this
   page cannot drift from the colours the map actually draws. */
const access = idx.access || {};
---
<Base
  title="Help"
  eyebrow="Searching · the colours · when it finds nothing"
  dek="Find a place whose name has changed, read the colour of a dot, and know what to do when the answer is nothing.">

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Four ways to search</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-grid hp-grid">
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">Aa</span><h3>A surname</h3><p>The map lights the countries where a register or archive records it. That is where to start, not proof your family lived there.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">⌂</span><h3>A village, by any name</h3><p>Gallignana goes to Gračišće, Breslau to Wrocław, Memel to Klaipėda. It works worldwide, not only where the shelf is deep.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">+</span><h3>A name and a place</h3><p><em>Blazevic Gracisce</em> narrows to that name on that ground.</p></li>
    <li class="k-card"><span class="k-ico" aria-hidden="true">◎</span><h3>Click a country</h3><p>Every country answers with something: whose national archive, what research guide exists.</p></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>What the colour of a dot means</h2><span class="k-count">what it costs to look</span></div>
  <ul class="k-grid hp-key">
    {Object.entries(access).map(([k, v]) => (
      <li class="k-card" style={`--dot: var(--acc-${k}, var(--acc-unsurveyed))`}><h3><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{k}</h3><p>{v}</p></li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p class="k-lede hp-lede">“Online” is eight different things, not one, and the last of these is the commonest colour on the map.
    Set a year and the map also says whose archive held that ground: <a href={u("/providers/#regions")}>the table behind that</a>.</p>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>When it finds nothing</h2></div>
  <div class="k-hi"><p><b>A grey dot means nobody has surveyed it, not that nothing is there.</b></p></div>
  <ol class="k-steps">
    <li><b>Set the year.</b> See whose archive held that ground. The records may be filed under a country you were not searching.</li>
    <li><b>Open the source directory</b> for that country and write to the archive named there. <a href={u("/providers/")}>The sources →</a></li>
    <li><b>Try the newspapers.</b> For some countries, Australia above all, a newspaper is the record.</li>
    <li><b>Found it?</b> <a href={u("/add/")}>Send it back.</a> A grey dot you turned into an answer is the most valuable thing a stranger can give this map.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>What it does not know yet</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-pills hp-stats">
    <li><span class="k-pill is-solid">{unsurveyedPct}% never surveyed</span></li>
    <li><span class="k-pill"><b>{archives.length}</b> archives in <b>{archiveCountries}</b> countries</span></li>
    <li><span class="k-pill"><b>{places.toLocaleString()}</b> places</span></li>
    <li><span class="k-pill"><b>{volumes.toLocaleString()}</b> volumes</span></li>
    <li><span class="k-pill"><b>{regions.regions.length}</b> jurisdiction regions</span></li>
  </ul>
  <p class="k-lede hp-lede">The shelf is deep in one corner: Croatia, Istria and Carnia are far ahead. The jurisdiction layer covers
    {regions.regions.length} pieces of ground, not the planet, and a place outside them says so rather than guessing. A confident wrong answer about which archive to write to costs somebody a month.</p>

  {/* WHAT THE ATLAS IS, IN WORDS: it sat under the map on the home page until 23 Nov 2026, when David asked for the map to have the room. */}
  <HomeAbout />

  <div class="k-bar"><h2>Still stuck?</h2></div>
  <ul class="k-pills">
    <li><a class="k-pill" href={u("/start/")}>Start here</a></li>
    <li><a class="k-pill is-plain" href={u("/coverage/")}>What’s missing</a></li>
  </ul>
</Base>

<style>
  .hp-grid .k-card { align-items: flex-start; }
  .hp-grid h3 { font-size: 20px; }
  .hp-key { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 220px), 1fr)); }
  .hp-key .k-card { border-top-color: var(--dot); border-radius: 14px; padding: 12px 14px; }
  .hp-key h3 { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; font: 700 12px/1.2 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); }
  .hp-key h3 i { width: 14px; height: 14px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--dot); border: 2px solid var(--ink-2); box-sizing: border-box; flex: none; }
  .hp-lede { margin: 14px 0 6px; }
  .hp-stats { margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .hp-stats .k-pill { font-size: 14px; padding: 6px 14px; }
  main .k-steps > li::before { background: var(--hue-wash); color: var(--hue-ink); border-color: var(--hue); }
</style>
